error[E0282]: `doubled` is `@no_alloc`, but `[x * 2 for x in xs]` may allocate
  --> no_alloc_run.sisu:6:12
  |
6 |     return [x * 2 for x in xs]
  |            ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
  = fix: take the list as a `mut` parameter, made by the caller where allocating is allowed, and set its elements in place without growing it
  = fix: remove `@no_alloc`, so that `doubled` may allocate

error[E0400]: `xs` was moved on line 10 and cannot be used afterwards
  --> no_alloc_run.sisu:11:19
   |
11 |     print(doubled(xs))
   |                   ^^
   |
10 |     let ys = xs
   |              -- `xs` is moved here
  = note: copy it with `.copy()` before the move, which makes a second value (for a list or a `String`, an allocation); move it later, after its last use, which costs nothing; or, where what it moves into only reads it, take it there without `own`, and the call lends it

